  data: {
    LLM: "Game: Queen's Slipper 500. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.",
    Player: "Queen's Slipper 500 is the definitive Australian version of the card game 500, played using specialized decks produced by the iconic Queen's Slipper brand. While standard 500 exists, the Australian variant is unique for its use of 11s, 12s, and 13s, allowing for 4, 5, or even 6-player games with expanded decks. It is a trick-taking game that evolved from Euchre, featuring a complex bidding system, the 'MisÃ¨re' (no-trick) contract, and the inclusion of a Joker as the ultimate trump card.",
    objective: 'Be the first team to reach 500 points or force opponents to -500 points.',
    gameplay: 'Partners sit opposite. Deal 10 each and 3 to kitty. Bid from six tricks in a suit or No Trumps, or Misere (lose every trick) or Open Misere. Highest bidder takes kitty, discards three, and leads. Follow suit; trick to highest trump or highest of led suit. Joker is highest trump; Right and Left Bower next. First team to 500 wins; minus 500 loses.',
    keyRules: [
      'Bidding order: Spades lowest, Clubs, Diamonds, Hearts, No Trumps. Misere only after someone bid seven. Contractor picks up kitty and discards three. Must follow suit. Trick winner leads next. Opponents score 10 per trick taken when contractors make contract.',
